Z||000002||dogtired||12-15-1999||05:20 PM||||In todays terms, I say hay look at that POS (Piece of S#$t)   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Ok there are other slang terms such as:<BR>Mexican socket set  means Crecent wrench!<BR>how bout:<BR>Mexican Drag Slicks  means Bald tires!<BR>These are just a few off the top of my head, OK who took my medication?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><P>Disclamer: No inference is being made to any one on this list or not. I do not take any responsibility for any of my comments I make  and will try and blame the clocest person standing to me. Therefore if you want to call me a mexican, indian, irish, jew, french, canadian, european or whatever that is cool, I walk on all fours like the rest of you!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ||||reg||6
Z||000003||william_thorniii||12-15-1999||06:04 PM||||Fans of cars of the fifties will never forget the Lead Sleds... which usually refer to 49-52 Mercs.  The reasoning behind it was the Lead body filler.  Which is also the reason that most old body men are a little strange.  I guess they didn't discover a close proximity to lead was bad for people until later.  At least lets hope so.<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||1
