Z||000019||Monkeyman||12-16-1999||04:07 PM||||What's up with the hydraulics, anyway?  I think it's kinda stupid.  (Although it might make it easier to change a tire on a low-rider.)  I could see putting something like that on a lowered car just in case you needed the extra ground clearance (snow?), but I don't understand it for looks.  And, while we're on the subject, what's with the bouncing they do?  Seems like that would be hard on the car (and the driver).  Just some thoughts.||||reg||1
